  "body": "Public documentation now works before console authentication. Audience links and stable section anchors support local developers and operators. The documentation layout uses readable text, bounded line width, and keyboard-accessible code blocks. Settings retain the responsive layout from current main.\n\nThe README adds offline catalog exploration and a bounded streaming request. The performance guide distinguishes the existing controller timer from complete gateway latency. A full HTTP measurement fixture covers authentication and direct-versus-proxied requests.\n\nThe native release workflow verifies published Starport archives on Windows, Linux, and macOS, with x86-64 and ARM64 runners. This PR supports the active production catalog plan. Production qualification and the released Starmap/Starport pair remain open.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 457 console tests across 74 files, TypeScript checks, and console build passed after integration with main.\n- All Go tests and vet passed. App and controller race tests passed.\n- The repository pre-PR checks passed, including first-run startup and Python, TypeScript, and Go SDK smoke tests.\n- Eight native-release verifier tests passed. Six native hosted checks passed before the current base update.\n\n\n\nCurrent merge scope (2026-09-08)\n\nThis PR retains stable Starmap `v0.16.5`.\nIt now includes main after PRs #367 and #368.\nFresh checks run at head `2973fd08122bc8264c499b99e60b44c890f3c6c7`.\nThe published documentation, performance fixture, and native workflow can merge when those checks pass.\n\nSix later local commits through 69b5aff remain outside this PR. They cover Compose persistence, the recorded README demonstration, integration fixtures, and the Starmap candidate dependency. Their release contract still requires a compatible stable Starmap tag. They retain their separate evidence and required publication review.\n",
